      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301816",
      ":question/problem": "A transportation researcher recorded the commuting distance of a random sample of employees at a company. Based on the data, the estimated mean commuting distance was $15.2$ miles, with a margin of error of $1.4$ miles.\n\nGiven this information, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. It is plausible that the mean commuting distance for all employees is between $13.8$ miles and $16.6$ miles.\n2. It is possible that some employees commute less than $12$ miles.\n3. It is **NOT** possible that some employees commute $17$ miles or more."
    },
