      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-302064",
      ":question/problem": "A fitness coach measured the average daily step count of a random sample of office workers. Based on the data, the estimated mean daily step count was $7,800$ steps, with a margin of error of $400$ steps.\n\nGiven this information, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. It is plausible that the mean daily step count for all office workers is between $7,400$ steps and $8,200$ steps.\n2. Some office workers may have a daily step count lower than $7,400$ steps.\n3. Some office workers may have a daily step count higher than $8,200$ steps."
    }
